If a clinician continues an opioid-therapy for a patient then it is recommended that the clinician collaborates with the patient for an opioid-continuation-benefit-risk-evaluation and evaluates an opioid-continuation-benefit and evaluates an opioid-continuation-risk and carefully weighs the opioid-continuation-benefit against the opioid-continuation-risk.
If a clinician increases an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully increase the opioid-dosage.
If a clinician continues an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully continue the opioid-dosage.
If a clinician reduces an opioid-dosage for a patient then the clinician should carefully reduce the opioid-dosage.
